  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The study introduces the Retrieval-Augmented Policy Analysis Framework (RAPAF), a system built with LangChain and ChatGPT to extract and analyze policy, strategy, and action items from climate equity and action plans. It also evaluates planning-related job postings to assess the demand for AI skills versus traditional planning roles, and implements a content-based recommendation system to identify semantic similarities in climate policies across different cities.",
      "why": "It demonstrates how large language models can automate the comparison of complex, unstructured policy documents across jurisdictions, allowing planners to quickly find cities with similar policy themes and strategies without manual coding."
    }
